window.ASAP_IFRC={"asof":"2026-10-05 18:10Z","src":"https://go.ifrc.org/","items":[{"id":8098,"name":"COD: Flooding - 09-2026 - Floods in Luiza territory, Kasai Central province (DRC)","type":"Flood","start":"2026-09-27","ccs":["cd"],"affected":null,"summary":"In the middle of the rainy season in the province of Kasai-Central, the territory of Luiza was hit by a violent torrential rain on the night of Saturday 26 to Sunday 27 September 2026. The bad weather caused many victims as well as considerable material and infrastructure damage. On a human level, the situation remains extremely worrying. A total of 12,000 households are homeless, having lost everything in the disaster. The bad weather caused the total destruction of 1,500 homes and partial dama","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8098"},{"id":8094,"name":"LBY: Pluvial/Flash Flood - 09-2026 - Sokna Flood ","type":"Pluvial/Flash Flood","start":"2026-09-22","ccs":["ly"],"affected":null,"summary":"شهدت ليبيا خلال الأسبوع الماضي حالة من التقلبات الجوية الخريفية وعدم الاستقرار ، ترافقت مع أمطار رعدية متفاوتة الشدة، كانت غزيرة محلياً في عدد من مناطق الشمال والجنوب والوسط. وشملت التحذيرات مناطق جبل نفوسة، وغدامس، وغات، ووادي الشاطئ، وهون، وزلة والهروج، إضافة إلى أجزاء من الجبل الأخضر ودرنة. وأشارت النشرات الجوية إلى ارتفاع مخاطر تجمع المياه في المناطق المنخفضة وحدوث سيول مفاجئة وجريان للأودية ، خاصة أثناء نشاط الخلايا الرعدية. وأدت هذه الظروف إلى آثار إنسانية مباشرة في عدد من المناطق. ففي منط","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8094"},{"id":8093,"name":"VNM: Flood - 09-2026 - Heavy rainfall ","type":"Flood","start":"2026-09-21","ccs":["vn"],"affected":null,"summary":"According to local authorities and online sources, heavy rainfall has caused flooding across northern and north-central Viet Nam. The Department of Dyke Management and Disaster Prevention and Control reported on 21 September 2026 that three deaths remain confirmed in Phu Tho. Eight houses had collapsed and 144 were damaged. Approximately 3,462 houses remained flooded, mainly in Ha Noi and Ninh Binh, down from 5,099 in the previous report. The latest assessment recorded 10,120 ha of rice and othe","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8093"},{"id":8097,"name":"THA: Flood - 09-2026 - Heavy rainfall caused flooding ","type":"Flood","start":"2026-09-16","ccs":["th"],"affected":null,"summary":"Thailand has experienced widespread flooding following heavy rainfall during 16&ndash;28 September 2026. According to the Department of Disaster Prevention and Mitigation(DDPM) report, flooding affected 41 provinces, covering 214 districts, 1,017 sub-districts and 5,164 vilages, with approximately 927,400 households (2,561,569 people) affected. A total of 23 deaths were reported, with no injuries recorded. As of 28 September, flooding remained ongoing in 28 provinces, covering 160 districts, 849","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8097"},{"id":8090,"name":"Bangladesh: Dengue Outbreak, 2026","type":"Epidemic","start":"2026-09-14","ccs":["bd"],"affected":null,"summary":"Dengue remains a major public health concern in Bangladesh, with recurrent seasonal outbreaks that threaten life and stretch the health system's capacity. The 2026 outbreak has followed an unusual trajectory: national figures ran below the 2025 pace through mid-August, before a sharp monsoon-driven surge from late August pushed the cumulative case count past last year's comparable tally within weeks. According to the Directorate General of Health Services (DGHS), from the beginning of the year t","appeals":[{"code":"MDRBD041","type":"DREF","amount":494769}],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8090"},{"id":8095,"name":"COD: Epidemic - 09-2026 - The Democratic Republic of Congo is facing the cholera epidemic on the rise nationwide.","type":"Epidemic","start":"2026-09-14","ccs":["cd"],"affected":null,"summary":"The Democratic Republic of the Congo is facing an upward trend in the cholera epidemic at the national level. In week 37, the country recorded about 2,200 suspected cases and 14 deaths across different health zones. The cumulative toll for 2026 now exceeds 41,300 suspected cases and 1,214 deaths reported on the national territory. A total of 16 of the 26 provinces of the DRC have reported outbreaks or active cases since the beginning of the year. In week 38, the National Institute of Public Heal","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8095"},{"id":8087,"name":"ARG: Cyclone - 09-2026 - Severe Storms","type":"Cyclone","start":"2026-09-11","ccs":["ar"],"affected":null,"summary":"During the afternoon, a severe weather phenomenon affected a rural area of the municipality of San Pedro, province of Misiones, between Cruce Caballero – at km 1072 – and Piñalito Sur. According to preliminary information, one person died and several homes suffered serious damage, including partial destruction and blowing off roofs. Damage to power lines, power and communications interruptions, and damage to rural roads were also reported. Police, municipal and provincial authorities are carryin","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8087"},{"id":8089,"name":"COD: Population displacement - 09-2026 - Population movement in the village of KINTYA in the territory of Mitwaba, Haut-Katanga province","type":"Population Movement","start":"2026-09-11","ccs":["cd"],"affected":null,"summary":"The territory of Mitwaba remains one of the main hotbeds of instability in Haut-Katanga, marked by the recurrent activism of the Mai-Mai Bakata Katanga. The year 2026 was marked by two major incursions confirmed by the authorities and by a deterioration in security around the Upemba National Park. At present, a new incursion by the Mai-Mai was reported this morning, Friday, September 11, 2026, at around 4 a.m. Sharp clashes are taking place between him and elements of the regular army in the vil","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8089"},{"id":8086,"name":"COD: Fire - 09-2026 - Series of fires in Bukavu in the province of South Kivu in the DRC","type":"Fire","start":"2026-09-10","ccs":["cd"],"affected":null,"summary":"A series of devastating fires has hit three health areas in the city of Bukavu (Buholo-Kasha, Mosala and Chimpunda), causing significant material damage and heavy loss of life. The first fire broke out during school hours on Nyabwanda Avenue, in the Buholo-Kasha neighborhood of Bagira commune. A kitchen fire left unattended is believed to have caused the fire in a house located in the immediate vicinity of the Furaha and Ujamaa school complexes. The fire then quickly spread to Maendeleo Avenue (","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8086"},{"id":8088,"name":"DJI: Population Movement - 09-2026","type":"Population Movement","start":"2026-09-10","ccs":["dj"],"affected":null,"summary":"Since 10 September 2026, the Obock region has been experiencing a significant influx of people arriving from Yemen, amid a deteriorating security and humanitarian situation in the country. According to estimates shared by ONARS, approximately 1,600 Yemeni refugees , mainly women and children, have arrived in the Obock region to date. Some individuals are reported to have been rescued at sea by the Djiboutian authorities after their boats ran out of fuel. The main arrival points identified are Ob","appeals":[{"code":"MDRDJ011","type":"DREF","amount":749935}],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8088"},{"id":8085,"name":"BGD: Epidemic - 09-2026 - Dengue in Bangladesh ","type":"Epidemic","start":"2026-09-09","ccs":["bd"],"affected":null,"summary":"The current dengue outbreak is placing substantial pressure on Bangladesh's health system, particularly in high-burden districts and urban centres. As of 8 September 2026, more than 45,000 dengue cases and 130 deaths had been reported nationwide, with over 1,500 new cases recorded in a single day and admissions continuing to rise. The surge in severe and hospitalized cases is increasing demand for hospital beds, clinical staff, diagnostics, blood transfusion services, and essential treatment sup","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8085"},{"id":8080,"name":"IDN: Volcanic Eruption - 09-2026 - Situation Report: Escalation of Volcanic Activity at Mt. Krakatau, Sunda Strait ","type":"Volcanic Eruption","start":"2026-09-04","ccs":["id"],"affected":null,"summary":"Situation Overview: Mt. Krakatau Volcanic Activity Background and Alert Status Mt. Krakatau, located in the Sunda Strait, has shown a significant escalation in volcanic activity since early July 2026. Following a prolonged period of dormancy, activity intensified, prompting the Geological Agency to raise the alert status from Level II (Waspada/Caution) to Level III (Siaga/Alert) on July 2, 2026. Eruption Timeline Based on monitoring by the Geological Agency, the eruption commenced on Friday (04/","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8080"},{"id":8081,"name":"BIH: Fire - 09-2026 - BiH: Fire_092026 ","type":"Fire","start":"2026-09-04","ccs":["ba"],"affected":null,"summary":"Wildfires have been affecting large parts of Bosnia and Herzegovina since early August 2026, with the situation particularly severe in Herzegovina, where NASA fire-detection systems recorded 1,292 hotspots in just the first 13 days of August &mdash; three times more than in the same period last year. The 2026 fire season has been driven by prolonged drought, high temperatures and strong, shifting winds, resulting in numerous simultaneous wildfires across both entities. Currently active fires (as","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8081"},{"id":8083,"name":"YEM: Other - 09-2026 - Yemen-Conflict Escalation, Mass Dispalacement and Health Impact","type":"Other","start":"2026-09-03","ccs":["ye"],"affected":null,"summary":"Since 3 September 2026, an escalation of hostilities in Taiz and along Yemen’s western coast has resulted in civilian casualties, new and secondary displacement, increased humanitarian needs and additional pressure on health services and receiving communities. Based on currently available information, YRCS estimates a gross displaced caseload of 4,362 households (26,075 people) across Taiz, Al Hodeidah and Aden. The displacement situation remains fluid, with further population movements possible","appeals":[{"code":"MDRYE018","type":"Emergency Appeal","amount":15000000}],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8083"},{"id":8091,"name":"ZMB: Epidemic - 08-2026 - Anthrax ","type":"Epidemic","start":"2026-08-31","ccs":["zm"],"affected":null,"summary":"On 31 August 2026, the District Health Office received a report of three suspected human anthrax cases from Kazembe and Kalimba, accompanied by reports of animals dying from suspected anthrax in the Munyamazi River area. In response, a multidisciplinary Rapid Response Team (RRT) was constituted to investigate the situation, assess the extent of the suspected outbreak, and identify possible sources of exposure. The RRT comprised representatives from the Ministry of Livestock and Fisheries, Depart","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8091"},{"id":8076,"name":"PHL: Flood - 08-2026 - PHL: Enhanced by Southwest Monsoon (Habagat) ","type":"Flood","start":"2026-08-29","ccs":["ph"],"affected":null,"summary":"The Southwest Monsoon (Habagat) has intensified over the Philippines, bringing persistent and at times heavy to intense rainfall over western and northern Luzon, Metro Manila, and parts of MIMAROPA and the Visayas. The enhanced monsoon is being further influenced by an two LPAs east of Extreme Northern Luzon, which may develop into a tropical cyclone and is expected to continue enhancing the Habagat. As of 29 August 2026, PAGASA has issued multiple heavy rainfall warnings, including Red Warning ","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8076"},{"id":8073,"name":"Nepal: Rasuwa Flash Flood, 2026","type":"Flood","start":"2026-08-26","ccs":["np"],"affected":84270,"summary":"A major flash flood struck Rasuwa district after a sudden and intense surge in the Bhote Koshi River at approximately 9:15 AM . The flood rapidly impacted the Timure, Rasuwagadhi, and Syabrubesi areas, causing significant damage to settlements, markets, police infrastructure, roads, and hydropower facilities. Authorities have warned that rising water levels could affect downstream communities along the Trishuli River corridor . Current Situation The flood is suspected to have originated from a h","appeals":[{"code":"MDRNP022","type":"Emergency Appeal","amount":18000000}],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8073"},{"id":8074,"name":"IND: Flood - 08-2026 - Bihar Floods - 2026 ","type":"Flood","start":"2026-08-26","ccs":["in"],"affected":null,"summary":"\"Bihar on Alert in View of Possible Flash Flood in the Gandak River\"","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8074"},{"id":8075,"name":"SLV: Drought - 08-2026 - Hydrological Drought - El Salvador ","type":"Drought","start":"2026-08-26","ccs":["sv"],"affected":null,"summary":"According to data from the Ministry of Environment and Natural Resources, meteorological and hydrological drought is expected at the national level, emphasizing effects in the area of dry corridor formed by the departments of La Unión, Usulután, San Miguel and Morazán, in view of this situation the General Directorate of Civil Protection issues a RED ALERT for drought conditions at the national level.","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8075"},{"id":8069,"name":"VNM: Cyclone - 08-2026 - Typhoon Narra ","type":"Cyclone","start":"2026-08-22","ccs":["vn"],"affected":null,"summary":"Storm Narra, the fourth to hit the East Sea this year, brought strong winds and heavy rains to northern Việt Nam early on August 22, with some areas forecast to receive more than 500mm of rain as the storm moves slowly over the northern waters of the East Sea. According to the National Centre for Hydrometeorological Forecasting, early on August 22, strong winds of level eight (62-74 km/h), with gusts up to level nine, were recorded at Bạch Long Vĩ special zone in Hải Ph&ograve;ng city, while win","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8069"},{"id":8082,"name":"Honduras - Drought Assessment","type":"Drought","start":"2026-08-21","ccs":["hn"],"affected":null,"summary":"Since May 2026, Honduras has been facing a progressive deterioration in climatic conditions associated with the delay in the start of the rainy season, the irregular distribution of rainfall, high temperatures, and the influence of the El Niño phenomenon. According to the Center for Atmospheric, Oceanographic and Seismic Studies (CENAOS), during May precipitation deficits of more than 50% were recorded in sectors of the center and south of the country; In June, the impact extended to municipalit","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8082"},{"id":8071,"name":"PER: Earthquake - 08-2026 - SISMO DE MAGNITUD 7.2 CON EPICENTRO EN EL DISTRITO DE CORACORA - AYACUCHO ","type":"Earthquake","start":"2026-08-20","ccs":["pe"],"affected":null,"summary":"De acuerdo con el Reporte Complementario N.&ordm; 11027 del COEN-INDECI (23 de agosto de 2026, 19:50 h; Reporte N.&ordm; 10), el 20 de agosto de 2026 a las 13:00:16 horas se registr&oacute; un sismo con epicentro localizado a 35 km al norte de Coracora, provincia de Parinacochas, departamento de Ayacucho, a una profundidad de 108 km (latitud -14.70&deg;, longitud -73.78&deg;), con una intensidad estimada de III-IV en Coracora. Debido a su car&aacute;cter profundo, el movimiento s&iacute;smico fu","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8071"},{"id":8101,"name":"Guinea-Bissau - Windstorm 2026","type":"Other","start":"2026-08-19","ccs":["gw"],"affected":null,"summary":"","appeals":[{"code":"MDRGW009","type":"DREF","amount":213481}],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8101"},{"id":8068,"name":"Liberia : Floods - 08-2026","type":"Flood","start":"2026-08-19","ccs":["lr"],"affected":null,"summary":"Since August 19, 2026, there has been sustained heavy rainfall consistent with the Liberia rainy season, which has caused widespread flash and riverine flooding across seven counties: Montserrado, Cape Mount, Grand Bassa, Bomi, Bong, Rivergss, and Nimba. Montserrado, home to Monrovia ( Liberia's Capital), has a dense urban corridor and the epicenter, with informal settlements along the St. Paul River, StocktonCreek, Du River, and the Mesurado River. Wetlands especially exposed to slow-draining f","appeals":[{"code":"MDRLR012","type":"DREF","amount":462836}],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8068"},{"id":8078,"name":"NGA: Population Movement - 08-2026","type":"Population Movement","start":"2026-08-18","ccs":["ng"],"affected":null,"summary":"A joint rapid assessment conducted by the Nigerian Red Cross Society (NRCS), SEMA and Médecins Sans Frontières (MSF) from 28–31 August 2026 has identified continued and expanding population movements in Danko-Wasagu and Sakaba LGAs in Zuru Emirate, Kebbi State, confirming that the emerging displacement situation extends beyond the initially affected locations. The assessment is part of ongoing efforts to establish the scale and humanitarian needs of displaced and host populations following recen","appeals":[{"code":"MDRNG047","type":"DREF","amount":744857}],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8078"},{"id":8064,"name":"NGA: Flood - 08-2026 - Flood – Ondo State, Nigeria ","type":"Flood","start":"2026-08-17","ccs":["ng"],"affected":null,"summary":"Sustained and heavy rainfall across Ondo State beginning in early August 2026 has triggered widespread riverine and urban flooding across at least seven Local Government Areas in the state, inundating homes, submerging roads and bridges, destroying property and displacing large numbers of residents. The flooding is ongoing and worsening, with multiple communities in the riverine south of the state particularly severely affected as water levels continue to rise. The situation in Ilaje Local Gover","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8064"},{"id":8062,"name":"PAN: Flood - 08-2026 - Bocas del Toro Floods ","type":"Flood","start":"2026-08-16","ccs":["pa"],"affected":null,"summary":"During the afternoon of Sunday, August 16, 2026, the National Civil Protection System (SINAPROC) declared a Green Alert for rain, storms and gusts of wind , starting at 6:00 p.m., for sectors of the province of Bocas del Toro, the Ngäbe-Buglé Region and the Naso Tjër Di Region. The measure is based on the technical-scientific analysis of the Institute of Meteorology and Hydrology of Panama (IMHPA), which maintains a favorable scenario for rains of varying intensity, some accompanied by thunderst","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8062"},{"id":8060,"name":"Indonesia: East Nusa Tenggara Earthquake, 2026","type":"Earthquake","start":"2026-08-15","ccs":["id"],"affected":null,"summary":"A magnitude 7.7 earthquake struck offshore Nagekeo Regency, East Nusa Tenggara Province, on 15 August 2026 at 04:58 WIB. The epicentre was located approximately 30 kilometres northeast of Mbay at a depth of 15 kilometres. The earthquake triggered a tsunami warning, which was lifted at 07:31 WIB after sea-level changes were detected in several coastal areas. The earthquake affected seven regencies in East Nusa Tenggara : Manggarai, East Manggarai, West Manggarai, Sikka, Ende, Nagekeo and Ngada. I","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8060"},{"id":8065,"name":"CRI: Flooding - 08-2026 - Floods due to the passage of Tropical Waves","type":"Flood","start":"2026-08-15","ccs":["cr"],"affected":null,"summary":"As of August 13, 2026, Costa Rica experienced a progressive increase in atmospheric instability, particularly over the Northern Zone and the Caribbean Slope, as a result of the interaction between the Intertropical Convergence Zone (ITCZ), a high moisture content and the successive transit of tropical waves. Given the expected deterioration of weather conditions, the National Commission for Risk Prevention and Emergency Response (CNE) initially declared a green alert for the Northern Zone and th","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8065"},{"id":8061,"name":"NGA: Flood - 08-2026 - Nigeria: Flood – Lafia, Nasarawa State ","type":"Flood","start":"2026-08-14","ccs":["ng"],"affected":null,"summary":"In the early hours of Wednesday, 13 August 2026, between approximately 4:42am and 8:39am, a heavy downpour struck Lafia, the capital of Nasarawa State, triggering severe urban flooding across four communities in Lafia Local Government Area: Bukansidi, Millionaires Quarters, Sadaji Junction/Police B Division and the Makurdi Road/Local Government Secretariat area. The intense and sustained rainfall overwhelmed the area's inadequate drainage infrastructure, causing floodwaters to inundate residenti","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8061"},{"id":8057,"name":"Philippines: Southwest Monsoon enhanced by Tropical Cyclones Maymay and Dolphin, 2026","type":"Cyclone","start":"2026-08-13","ccs":["ph"],"affected":null,"summary":"At 8:00 PM on 4 August 2026, the Low-Pressure Area (LPA) located west of Bacnotan, La Union intensified into Tropical Depression MAYMAY, according to the Philippine Atmospheric, Geophysical and Astronomical Services Administration (PAGASA). By 2:00 AM on 5 August 2026, Tropical Depression MAYMAY further intensified into Tropical Storm MAYMAY (international name: Kujira) while moving slowly near the western coast of Northern Luzon. On 6 August 2026, Tropical Storm MAYMAY weakened into a Tropical ","appeals":[{"code":"MDRPH060","type":"DREF","amount":409789}],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8057"},{"id":8059,"name":"NGA: Landslide - 08-2026 - Floods ","type":"Landslide","start":"2026-08-13","ccs":["ng"],"affected":null,"summary":"Weeks of continuous, unprecedented torrential rainfall across Calabar, the capital of Cross River State, have triggered devastating landslides and severe flooding across multiple communities in Calabar Municipality, resulting in loss of life, widespread destruction of homes and property, and the collapse of critical infrastructure. The rainfall, described by observers as unprecedented in scale and intensity for the city, has caused the terrain to collapse in several locations, destroying buildin","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8059"},{"id":8100,"name":"ZMB: Epidemic - 08-2026 - Cholera outbreak ","type":"Epidemic","start":"2026-08-13","ccs":["zm"],"affected":null,"summary":"The cholera outbreak is placing significant pressure on the health system and affected populations. The outbreak has increased the demand for cholera case management, surveillance, laboratory testing, emergency response and WASH services. As of 29 September 2026, seven districts across five provinces had reported 304 cases, including 62 laboratory-confirmed cases, with 35 patients receiving treatment and 11 reported deaths. The response has therefore required health workers and emergency teams t","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8100"},{"id":8055,"name":"Colombia - Earthquake 2026","type":"Earthquake","start":"2026-08-10","ccs":["co"],"affected":466644,"summary":"According to information from the Colombian Geological Service (SGC), an earthquake with a preliminary magnitude of 7.4 was recorded on Monday, August 10, 2026, in the morning, with its epicenter in the town of San José del Palmar, in the department of Chocó, located on the Colombian Pacific coast, at a depth of 96 kilometers. Although the epicenter was in the department of Chocó, direct impacts were also felt in the departments of Caldas, Risaralda, and Valle del Cauca. Media reports are alread","appeals":[{"code":"MDRCO036","type":"Emergency Appeal","amount":10000000}],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8055"},{"id":8053,"name":"URY: Cyclone - 08-2026 - Extratropical cyclone ","type":"Cyclone","start":"2026-08-06","ccs":["uy"],"affected":null,"summary":"The National Emergency System declares the Red Alert due to the formation of an extratropical cyclone, which will generate very strong and persistent winds, with very intense gusts that could exceed 120 km/h in the coastal strip between the Pando stream and the town of Aguas Dulces, from 9 p.m. today, Thursday, August 6, until 04:00 a.m. on Friday, August 7. What is the phenomenon that motivates the Red Alert? The Red Alert is declared due to the forecast of the formation of an extratropical cyc","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8053"},{"id":8044,"name":"URY: Flood - 08-2026 - Uruguay River Flood ","type":"Flood","start":"2026-08-04","ccs":["uy"],"affected":null,"summary":"Background Between the afternoon of Friday, July 31, and the early morning of Saturday, August 1, 2026, an episode of strong and occasionally severe storms was recorded in Uruguay, with greater impact in the northern part of the country. The event was associated with an orange level weather warning from INUMET and generated power outages, falling trees and minor damage to infrastructure, mainly concentrated in the department of Salto. As a result of the rains recorded in the upper and middle bas","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8044"},{"id":8043,"name":"LKA: Pluvial/Flash Flood - 08-2026 - South West Monsoon Activation 2026 ","type":"Pluvial/Flash Flood","start":"2026-08-03","ccs":["lk"],"affected":null,"summary":"Based on the current seasonal outlook and regional climate forecasts, Sri Lanka is expected to experience near-normal to slightly below-normal southwest monsoon rainfall, although rainfall distribution is likely to remain highly uneven with periods of heavy localized rain and dry spells. Emerging El Niño conditions may increasingly influence weather patterns during August–September 2026. The southwest monsoon is expected to continue with intermittent heavy rainfall events rather than persistent ","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8043"},{"id":8045,"name":"SLE: Pluvial/Flash Flood - 08-2026 - SLE: Flash Flood - 08-2026 - Freetown ","type":"Pluvial/Flash Flood","start":"2026-08-03","ccs":["sl"],"affected":null,"summary":"On the early morning of 3 August 2026, Freetown experienced approximately six to seven hours of continuous heavy rainfall, resulting in widespread flash flooding, severe erosion, and slope collapse incidents across several low-lying and hillside communities. The incidents caused significant damage to homes and infrastructure, displaced hundreds of people, resulted in fatalities and missing persons, and contaminated critical water sources. The National Disaster Management Agency (NDMA), together ","appeals":[{"code":"MDRSL022","type":"DREF","amount":370924}],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8045"},{"id":8046,"name":"GTM: Volcanic eruption - 08-2026 - Fuego Volcano Guatemala activity ","type":"Volcanic Eruption","start":"2026-08-03","ccs":["gt"],"affected":null,"summary":"According to the scientific entity of INSIVUMEH, constant monitoring of the development of the activity of the Fuego volcano has been maintained, confirming that seven hours have elapsed since its beginning (08:30 a.m. local time). The various monitoring parameters have been kept increasing progressively, confirming that there is still an intense emission of gases, volcanic ash and lava fragments from the crater. The ash and gas columns have reached 5000 to 6000 meters above sea level (14604 - 1","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8046"},{"id":8047,"name":"MNG: Flood - 08-2026 - Urban flood ","type":"Flood","start":"2026-08-01","ccs":["mn"],"affected":null,"summary":"Heavy rainfall on 1 August 2026 caused river and flash flooding in several parts of Ulaanbaatar, particularly in Khan-Uul and Songino-Khairkhan districts. The Tuul River exceeded the dangerous flood level and overflowed near the Biocombinat area, flooding homes, businesses, and public facilities. More than 190 people required rescue or evacuation assistance across at least three affected areas. Two children were found unconscious after being swept away by floodwater, received emergency first aid","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8047"},{"id":8042,"name":"GRC: Fire - 07-2026 - Attica Wildfire ","type":"Fire","start":"2026-07-31","ccs":["gr"],"affected":null,"summary":"A major wildfire broke out on Friday, 31 July 2026, near the coastal village of Agios Vasileios in Boeotia, before spreading rapidly southward. Authorities confirmed the wildfire was triggered by a spark from a power cable, and two employees of an electricity company were arrested over the blaze. Driven by strong to gale-force winds, the fire developed multiple active fronts and merged into a single, largely uncontrollable blaze. At its peak, the fire front stretched nearly 100 kilometers, from ","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8042"},{"id":8036,"name":"ISR: Complex Emergency - 07-2026 - Extreme Heat - High Temperatures ","type":"Complex Emergency","start":"2026-07-30","ccs":["il"],"affected":null,"summary":"The entire country of Israel is bracing for a near term expected severe heat wave with temperatures expected to peak at 45-47 degrees centigrade. The heat index nationwide is expected to be 'high' to 'very high' and there exists a high risk of fires.","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8036"},{"id":8040,"name":"ESP: Population Movement - 07-2026 - Population Movement Ceuta ","type":"Population Movement","start":"2026-07-30","ccs":["es"],"affected":null,"summary":"On July 30&ndash;31, 2026, the Spanish enclave of Ceuta experienced the largest mass migration breach in its history. An estimated 40,000&ndash;60,000 people crossed the border from Morocco in less than 48 hours, swimming around the Tarajal breakwater or surging through border gates. The scale and speed of the arrivals have placed significant pressure on local reception capacities and emergency response services. Reports indicate that the situation has resulted in numerous rescue operations, inj","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8040"},{"id":8041,"name":"MAR: Population Movement - 07-2026 - Massive population movement at Bab Sebta ","type":"Population Movement","start":"2026-07-30","ccs":["ma"],"affected":null,"summary":"1. Executive Summary An exceptional population movement toward the Bab Sebta (Ceuta) border crossing has generated significant humanitarian needs on the Moroccan side of the border. The situation escalated rapidly between 30 and 31 July 2026, resulting in a major migration, humanitarian, and security crisis affecting both Morocco and the Spanish autonomous city of Ceuta. According to reports from the Moroccan Red Crescent (MRC) on ground, local information and international media sources, tens o","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8041"},{"id":8039,"name":"GRC: Fire - 07-2026 - Rethymno Wildfires, July 2026 ","type":"Fire","start":"2026-07-29","ccs":["gr"],"affected":null,"summary":"A major wildfire that broke out on 29 July 2026 in the Krya Vrysi area of the Municipality of Agios Vasileios, southern Rethymno, rapidly spread across multiple fronts due to extreme weather conditions, including strong winds reaching up to 7-8 Beaufort and locally higher gusts. The fire affected several communities and tourist areas along the southern coast of Crete, including Agia Galini, Melampes, Saktouria, Agios Georgios, Agios Pavlos, Triopetra, Ligres and Agia Paraskevi. The fire front ex","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8039"},{"id":8035,"name":"JPN: Earthquake - 07-2026 - 2026 Kumamoto Earthquake (M7.1) ","type":"Earthquake","start":"2026-07-28","ccs":["jp","oki"],"affected":null,"summary":"Overview A magnitude 7.1 earthquake struck Kumamoto Prefecture at 4:27 p.m. local time on 28 July 2026. A tsunami advisory was issued for the Ariake Sea and Yatsushiro Sea immediately after the earthquake and was lifted at 6:10 p.m. local time. Aftershocks continue to occur in the affected area. As of 8:00 p.m., more than 60 felt earthquakes had been recorded following the main shock. Japan Meteorological Agency has warned of the possibility of further strong earthquakes over the coming week, pa","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8035"},{"id":8037,"name":"India: Assam Flood, 2026","type":"Flood","start":"2026-07-27","ccs":["in"],"affected":null,"summary":"","appeals":[{"code":"MDRIN029","type":"DREF","amount":500000}],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8037"},{"id":8030,"name":"FRA: Fire - 07-2026 - Landes ","type":"Fire","start":"2026-07-24","ccs":["fr"],"affected":null,"summary":"Massive forest fire causing the evacuation of several municipalities","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8030"},{"id":8029,"name":"FRA: Fire - 07-2026 - Gironde ","type":"Fire","start":"2026-07-22","ccs":["fr"],"affected":null,"summary":"Forest fire causing massive evacuations of municipalities in the Gironde department.","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8029"},{"id":8033,"name":"ESP: Fire - 07-2026 - Central area ","type":"Fire","start":"2026-07-22","ccs":["es"],"affected":null,"summary":"Multiple large wildfires continue to affect central Spain, particularly the Community of Madrid, the Province of &Aacute;vila and neighbouring areas of Toledo. Due to the severity, scale and humanitarian impact of the emergency, Spanish authorities have declared Operational Situation Level 3 (National Interest Emergency), placing response operations under national coordination. The wildfire complex has burned more than 22,000 hectares across Madrid and &Aacute;vila. The fire affecting Madrid has","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8033"},{"id":8025,"name":"Afghanistan: Nuristan Flood, 2026","type":"Flood","start":"2026-07-20","ccs":["af"],"affected":null,"summary":"On Monday, 20 July 2026, at approximately 3:00 p.m. local time, a sudden flash flood struck the central areas of Nuristan Province following heavy and continuous rainfall. The low-lying areas and communities located along rivers and seasonal watercourses were the most severely affected. In Nuristan Province, the flash floods resulted in fatalities and injuries, while causing extensive damage to the central market, residential houses, public infrastructure, livelihoods and income sources, as well","appeals":[{"code":"MDRAF022","type":"DREF","amount":472770}],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8025"},{"id":8027,"name":"DZA: Fire - 07-2026 - Algeria: Wildfires – July 2026 ","type":"Fire","start":"2026-07-18","ccs":["dz"],"affected":null,"summary":"On 18 July 2026, the wildfire emergency in Algeria reached a significant operational peak, with 154 forest, vegetation and agricultural fires recorded within 24 hours across several wilayas. Of these, 138 fires were extinguished, while 16 remained active at the time of reporting. The fires affected northern, north-eastern, central and western Algeria, including Annaba, Souk Ahras, Skikda, Guelma, Bouira, M&eacute;d&eacute;a, Mila, Mascara, El Tarf, Jijel, S&eacute;tif, B&eacute;ja&iuml;a, Tlemce","appeals":[{"code":"MDRDZ015","type":"DREF","amount":499541}],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8027"},{"id":8020,"name":"URY: Other - 07-2026 - Severe Storms","type":"Other","start":"2026-07-17","ccs":["uy"],"affected":null,"summary":"Between the early hours of Thursday, July 16 and Saturday, July 18, 2026, a warm front followed by a humid and unstable air mass generated strong and occasionally severe storms in much of the Uruguayan territory, with greater intensity in the northern and eastern departments (Salto, Tacuarembó, Treinta y Tres, among others). The storms were organized in a Mesoscale Convective System (MCS), producing wind gusts of up to 129.5 km/h in Salto, hail, intense electrical activity and abundant rainfall ","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8020"},{"id":8022,"name":"MWI: Epidemic - 07-2026 - Measles Outbreak","type":"Epidemic","start":"2026-07-17","ccs":["mw"],"affected":null,"summary":"The measles outbreak in Nsanje District continues to worsen, affecting several communities, particularly those along the Malawi–Mozambique border. As of 17 July 2026, the district had recorded 188 suspected measles cases, including 76 laboratory-confirmed cases. Children under 15 years of age, particularly those younger than five years, are the most affected. Key drivers of the outbreak include low immunization coverage, delayed health-seeking behaviour, cross-border population movement, and inc","appeals":[{"code":"MDRMW027","type":"DREF","amount":208871}],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8022"},{"id":8016,"name":"VNM: Flood - 07-2026 - Heavy Rainfall, Flash Floods and Landslides in Northern Viet Nam ","type":"Flood","start":"2026-07-16","ccs":["vn"],"affected":null,"summary":"Persistent heavy rainfall continues to affect northern Viet Nam, particularly the northwestern mountainous provinces, increasing the risk of flash floods, landslides and localised flooding. According to the Viet Nam Disaster and Dyke Management Authority (VDDMA), rainfall recorded between 19:00 on 16 July and 08:00 on 17 July reached exceptionally high levels in several locations, including 240 mm in Chế Tạo (L&agrave;o Cai Province), 224.4 mm in Nậm Păm (Sơn La Province) and 126.6 mm in T&agrav","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8016"},{"id":8032,"name":"MKD: Biological Emergency - 07-2026 - Water Contamination Incident in Gostivar, North Macedonia ","type":"Biological Emergency","start":"2026-07-16","ccs":["mk"],"affected":null,"summary":"On 16 July 2026 , a public health emergency emerged in the Municipality of Gostivar after contamination of the municipal drinking water supply resulted in a large number of people experiencing acute gastrointestinal illness. The affected water supply serves the city of Gostivar and several surrounding settlements, with an estimated 35,000&ndash;40,000 people exposed to the disruption. More than 1,500 people sought medical attention after developing symptoms including diarrhoea, vomiting, abdomin","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8032"},{"id":8018,"name":"MAR: Fire - 07-2026 - Ouneine-Ijoukak Wildfire ","type":"Fire","start":"2026-07-15","ccs":["ma"],"affected":null,"summary":"On Wednesday, July 15, a wildfire has broken out in the forest area located between the mountainous communes of Ounaine, in Taroudant Province, and Ijoukak, in Al Haouz province, west-central and southwestern Morocco. The fire spread rapidly due to a combination of strong winds, high temperatures, and rugged mountainous terrain, increasing the risk to surrounding forest ecosystems and nearby communities. Early estimates indicated an affected area of 100 hectares. Emergency response operations we","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8018"},{"id":8070,"name":"IDN: Fire - 07-2026 - Indonesia: Forest Fires and Haze in Sumatra and Kalimantan ","type":"Fire","start":"2026-07-14","ccs":["id"],"affected":null,"summary":"Since mid-July 2026, forest and land fires have increased across parts of Sumatra and Kalimantan amid prolonged dry conditions and the peak of the dry season. The Government of Indonesia has prioritized response operations in six provinces: Riau, Jambi, South Sumatra, West Kalimantan, Central Kalimantan and South Kalimantan. Fires have also been reported in East and North Kalimantan. Fire suppression remains challenging, particularly in peatland areas and remote locations with limited access to ","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8070"},{"id":8014,"name":"KGZ: Pluvial/Flash Flood - 07-2026 - Nooken Mudflow ","type":"Pluvial/Flash Flood","start":"2026-07-13","ccs":["kg"],"affected":null,"summary":"Executive Summary On 13 July 2026 at approximately 19:30 local time, heavy short-duration rainfall in the mountainous areas of Nooken District, Jalal-Abad Oblast triggered mudflows affecting Kochkor-Ata city and surrounding villages. Two mudflow channels overflowed simultaneously: the Besh-Korgon channel inundated residential streets in Kochkor-Ata city and destroyed 3 electricity poles in the Besh-Korgon settlement; the Kara-Bulak channel flooded Ergesh Aliev village. Separate mudflows from hig","appeals":[{"code":"MDRKG022","type":"DREF","amount":172190}],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8014"},{"id":8038,"name":"TUN: Fire - 07-2026 - Tunisia Wildfires 2026","type":"Fire","start":"2026-07-12","ccs":["tn"],"affected":null,"summary":"The wave of fires in the Republic of Tunisia began on 1 June 2026, but reached a sharp peak from 12 July 2026 onward, continuing to the time of writing, coinciding with an exceptional heatwave in which temperatures reached close to 50°C in several governorates — including Kairouan, Jendouba, Gabès, Tozeur and Béja — while temperatures in the south-west reached around 49°C due to the hot, dry \"Chehili\" desert winds, according to the National Institute of Meteorology. The heatwave has been accompa","appeals":[{"code":"MDRTN013","type":"DREF","amount":406066}],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8038"},{"id":8011,"name":"TJK: Flood - 07-2026 - TJK: Flood and Mudflow Ayni district ","type":"Flood","start":"2026-07-11","ccs":["tj"],"affected":null,"summary":"1. Situation Overview On 11 July 2026 , following intense rainfall, flash floods and mudflows affected the villages of Darg and Kazdon in Shamtuch Jamoat , Ayni District, Sughd Region. Mudflows descended through the Surkhi, Kashak, and Jari river channels, causing significant damage to residential houses, public infrastructure, road networks, water supply systems, agricultural land, and private property. According to the official authorities, no fatalities or injuries have been reported . Damage","appeals":[{"code":"MDRTJ038","type":"DREF","amount":227462}],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8011"},{"id":8054,"name":"TKM: Heat Wave - 07-2026 - Heat  Wave ","type":"Heat Wave","start":"2026-07-10","ccs":["tm"],"affected":null,"summary":"Turkmenistan is experiencing a severe heatwave combined with hydrological drought conditions, affecting vulnerable communities across several regions of the country. The situation is part of a wider regional climate crisis impacting Central Asia, characterized by exceptionally high temperatures, prolonged dry conditions, and increasing pressure on water resources. According to national hydrometeorological observations and regional climate monitoring data: Daytime temperatures have consistently r","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8054"},{"id":8009,"name":"ZMB: Epidemic - 07-2026 - Measles outbreak ","type":"Epidemic","start":"2026-07-08","ccs":["zm"],"affected":null,"summary":"The index case was identified in Epidemiological Week 19: a 6-year-old female of Kapengela village who presented at Shangombo District Hospital with fever, maculopapular rash, cough, conjunctivitis and coryza, with unknown vaccination history. A specimen was confirmed positive for Measles IgM antibody by the UTH Virology Laboratory on 16th May 2026, formally declaring the outbreak. On 6th May 2026, the District received an unverified report of a parallel measles outbreak in Rivungu Municipality,","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8009"},{"id":8006,"name":"CHL: Pluvial flood / flood - 07-2026 - Hydrometeorological Event","type":"Pluvial/Flash Flood","start":"2026-07-07","ccs":["cl"],"affected":null,"summary":"On Tuesday, July 7, a front of intense rainfall with High Zero Isothermal impacted between the regions of Maule and Los Lagos, generating in some locations - mainly coastal - figures over 100 mm of precipitation in 24 hours, which generated flooding of local rivers, floods and mass removals. At 12:15 p.m. on Wednesday, July 8, the Meteorological Alert was canceled due to intense rainfall with high zero isotherm in areas of the regions of La Araucanía and Los Ríos, as well as the Meteorological A","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8006"},{"id":8007,"name":"CHL: Volcanic Eruption - 07-2026 - Volcanic Activity Nevados de Chillán","type":"Volcanic Eruption","start":"2026-07-06","ccs":["cl"],"affected":null,"summary":"1. SUMMARY OF THE SITUATION: According to the information provided by the Chilean Meteorological Directorate (DMC), the following weather warnings are in force for the Ñuble Region: Alert Prognosis Home End Notice A302-4 Normal to moderate rainfall in the foothills and mountain ranges. 08-07 10-07 Notice A303-3 Normal to moderate wind on the coast, coastal mountain range, valley, pre-mountain range and mountain range. 08-07 10-07 On the other hand, the National Geology and Mining Service (SERNAG","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8007"},{"id":8010,"name":"GEO: Pluvial/Flash Flood - 07-2026 - Floods in Dedoplistkaro ","type":"Pluvial/Flash Flood","start":"2026-07-06","ccs":["ge"],"affected":null,"summary":"Strong hail and wind damaged the villages of the municipality. The situation was particularly difficult in the village of Gamarjveba, the roofs of houses, power lines were damaged. There was heavy rain in all the villages of the municipality, but the village of Gamarjveba was particularly damaged, where the disaster toppled trees and damaged part of the power lines. The roads were closed, but the response was prompt, both from the municipal services, as well as the fire and rescue service. The h","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8010"},{"id":8003,"name":"PAN: Flood - 07-2026 - PAN: Flood -07-2026 Caused by heavy rains ","type":"Flood","start":"2026-07-03","ccs":["pa"],"affected":null,"summary":"From July 2 in the early hours of the morning in the province of Bocas del Toro there have been downpours of varying intensity with thunderstorms and gusts of wind, generating situations of risk. On July 3 at 9:00 a.m., the COEP was activated, establishing itself in the facilities of the National Police, at the moment the province of Bocas del Toro is in emergency due to the situations that have been registered in different areas of the province, mainly in the district of Changuinola, in where f","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8003"},{"id":7999,"name":"PRY: Flood - 07-2026 - Rising levels of the Paraná River - Cerrito ","type":"Flood","start":"2026-07-02","ccs":["py"],"affected":null,"summary":"During the last 24 hours, the level of the Paraná River registered an approximate increase of 40 cm as a result of the intense rains recorded in the upper basin. This rapid variation in the level of the river has begun to affect the district of Cerrito, department of Ñeembucú, mainly in the lowest areas and exposed to flooding. Local authorities and monitoring agencies continue to monitor hydrological evolution, considering the possibility of further increases in river levels if rainfall persist","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7999"},{"id":8000,"name":"PRY: Flood - 07-2026 - Rise in the levels of the Paraná River due to the opening of Itaipu gates ","type":"Flood","start":"2026-07-02","ccs":["py"],"affected":null,"summary":"The Paraná River is expected to continue to register a gradual increase in its level over the next few days. This increase responds to the intense rainfall that occurred in the Iguazú River basin, as well as to the flooding of the Itaipu Hydroelectric Dam. Although the authorities indicate that it is not currently an emergency situation, it is recommended to maintain constant monitoring of the evolution of the river level and reinforce preventive measures in riparian areas. Likewise, extreme cau","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8000"},{"id":7998,"name":"LAO: Flood - 07-2026 - Flooding Caused by Heavy Rainfall ","type":"Flood","start":"2026-07-01","ccs":["la"],"affected":null,"summary":"According to the Department of Meteorology and Hydrology (DMH), a tropical depression over the South China Sea is expected to strengthen the south-west monsoon, bringing widespread heavy rainfall, thunderstorms and strong winds across Lao PDR between 2 and 5 July 2026. The forecast indicates an increased risk of flash floods, riverine flooding and landslides, particularly in northern provinces. On 30 June 2026, heavy rainfall triggered the first flooding incidents of the 2026 rainy season in Bok","appeals":[{"code":"MDRLA012","type":"DREF","amount":500000}],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7998"},{"id":8002,"name":"VNM: Flood - 07-2026 - Typhoon No. 1 (Maysak) and Floods ","type":"Flood","start":"2026-07-01","ccs":["vn"],"affected":null,"summary":"According to local goverment, a tropical depression over the East Sea intensified into Typhoon No. 1 (Maysak) on 2 July 2026. As of 08:00 (local time) on 3 July, the typhoon was located approximately 110 km south of Hainan Island (China), moving westwards at around 5 km/h with maximum sustained winds of 62&ndash;74 km/h (Force 8) and gusts up to Force 10. The storm is forecast to strengthen as it approaches the Gulf of Tonkin, bringing strong winds, rough seas and heavy rainfall to northern Viet","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8002"},{"id":8005,"name":"THA: Flood - 07-2026 - Windstorm and Flooding caused by Typhoon Maysak ","type":"Flood","start":"2026-07-01","ccs":["th"],"affected":null,"summary":"The influence of Typhoon Maysak, combined with the southwest monsoon, has resulted in strong winds and heavy rainfall across several parts of Thailand. According to the Department of Disaster Prevention and Mitigation (DDPM), windstorm and flooding incidents were reported between 1 and 6 July 2026. Windstorm incidents were reported in six provinces&mdash;Ubon Ratchathani, Rayong, Chanthaburi, Trat, Satun and Krabi&mdash;affecting eight districts, 15 sub-districts and 25 villages. A total of 133 ","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/8005"},{"id":7964,"name":"CRI: Drought - 06-2026 - ENSO Phenomenon - El Niño Phase 2026-2027 ","type":"Drought","start":"2026-06-29","ccs":["cr"],"affected":null,"summary":"In the first days of May, in most climatic regions, accumulated rainfall values are lower than normal, a closing with deficit conditions of -50% was projected for this month in the North Pacific, while the Central Pacific, South Pacific and Central Valley with -20% decrease compared to the historical average. On May 21, the IMN issued a bulletin indicating that the ENSO phenomenon (El Niño Southern Oscillation), will influence the climate of Costa Rica for the remainder of 2026, in such a way th","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7964"},{"id":7995,"name":"BEN: Flood - 06-2026 - flood ","type":"Flood","start":"2026-06-29","ccs":["bj"],"affected":null,"summary":"Depuis la fin du mois de juin 2026, la commune de Lokossa est confront&eacute;e &agrave; de graves inondations ayant touch&eacute; plusieurs localit&eacute;s, entra&icirc;nant d'importants d&eacute;g&acirc;ts mat&eacute;riels, agricoles et sociaux ainsi qu'une d&eacute;gradation significative des conditions de vie des populations affect&eacute;es. &Agrave; la suite d'une mission de terrain, la Plateforme Communale de R&eacute;duction des Risques de Catastrophe et d'Adaptation aux Changements Cli","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7995"},{"id":7997,"name":"PAK: Pluvial/Flash Flood - 06-2026 - Pakistan Monsoon Floods, Situation Update ","type":"Pluvial/Flash Flood","start":"2026-06-28","ccs":["pk"],"affected":null,"summary":"The 2026 monsoon season has commenced across Pakistan, with the first spell of seasonal rains affecting several parts of the country and increasing the risk of flash floods, riverine flooding, landslides, and other weather-related hazards, particularly in vulnerable and mountainous areas. Rainfall continues across different parts of Pakistan, and according to the Pakistan Meteorological Department (PMD), widespread monsoon activity is expected to persist until 6 July 2026, with the possibility o","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7997"},{"id":7993,"name":"GEO: Flood - 06-2026 - Heavy Rain and Floods in Samegrelo and Zemo Svaneti Region ","type":"Flood","start":"2026-06-27","ccs":["ge"],"affected":null,"summary":"On 27 June 2026, continuous heavy rainfall triggered severe flooding in Senaki and Chkhorotsku municipalities in the Samegrelo-Zemo Svaneti Region. Heavy rainfall has continued without interruption since the early hours of 27 June, and as of 29 June the emergency situation remains ongoing. Due to the continuing rainfall and flooding, local authorities have not yet been able to complete a comprehensive damage assessment. According to preliminary estimates, approximately 600 households have been a","appeals":[{"code":"MDRGE021","type":"DREF","amount":223448}],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7993"},{"id":7991,"name":"ENG: Heatwave - 06-2026 - Heatwave ","type":"Heat Wave","start":"2026-06-26","ccs":["fr"],"affected":null,"summary":"This second heat wave began on June 20 with very high temperatures. This is the hottest and longest episode ever experienced since meteorological records began. Alert and maximum mobilization levels have been triggered throughout the country. No territory in metropolitan France is spared. The wave is long-lasting, disrupting daily activities, and causing the closure of schools and nurseries, the saturation of pre-hospital and hospital structures, the saturation of emergency numbers in some terri","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7991"},{"id":7990,"name":"Venezuela Earthquake","type":"Earthquake","start":"2026-06-24","ccs":["ve"],"affected":9730000,"summary":"On 24 June 2026, two strong earthquakes, preliminarily measured at magnitudes 7.1 and 7.5, struck north-central Venezuela in rapid succession, with epicentres near Morón, Carabobo State. The earthquakes were felt across much of the country, including Caracas, La Guaira, Aragua, Carabobo and neighbouring states. Therefore, the national goverment of Venezuela declared the state of emergency. Preliminary information indicates damage to residential and commercial buildings, with reports of structura","appeals":[{"code":"MDRVE015","type":"Emergency Appeal","amount":50000000}],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7990"},{"id":7982,"name":"IDN: Earthquake - 06-2026 - Central Sulawesi Earthquake – Magnitude 6.7 ","type":"Earthquake","start":"2026-06-16","ccs":["id"],"affected":null,"summary":"On 16 June 2026 at 10:27 WIB, a magnitude 6.7 earthquake struck Central Sulawesi Province at a depth of 10 km. The epicentre was located approximately 42 km southeast of Palu City (1.04&deg;S, 120.23&deg;E). According to the Meteorology, Climatology and Geophysics Agency (BMKG), the earthquake did not have tsunami potential. The shaking was strongly felt in Palu (MMI VI&ndash;VII) and Sigi (MMI V&ndash;VI), while light to moderate tremors were reported across several areas in Sulawesi, Kalimanta","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7982"},{"id":7989,"name":"Chad - 2026 Cholera Outbreak","type":"Epidemic","start":"2026-06-16","ccs":["td"],"affected":null,"summary":"The analysis of epidemiological data and field observations reveals the following elements: An epidemic that is still localized but at risk of spread With 52 confirmed cases out of a total population of 124,300 inhabitants, the apparent overall attack rate remains low. However, this ratio is misleading: cases are concentrated in only 3 of the district's 14 areas of responsibility, meaning that the actual attack rate in the affected areas is significantly higher than the district average suggests","appeals":[{"code":"MDRTD026","type":"DREF","amount":375000}],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7989"},{"id":7987,"name":"COG: Displacement - 06-2026 - MOVEMENT OF THE POPULATION OF THE DRC IN THE REPUBLIC OF CONGO","type":"Population Movement","start":"2026-06-15","ccs":["cg"],"affected":null,"summary":"On 3 November 2025, a latent land dispute between the Lobalatanda and Engalango Sud communities, in the Dongo sector (Sud-Ubangi, DRC), degenerated into violence after the murder of a teacher perceived as a triggering act. The clashes left five dead, thirteen injured and burned nearly fifty houses around Tomba, forcing residents to flee. In a few days, 3,500 households (17,500 people) crossed the river to take refuge in the Republic of Congo, mainly in Bétou, Enyellé and riverside villages such ","appeals":[{"code":"MDRCG029","type":"DREF","amount":499825}],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7987"},{"id":7977,"name":"IDN: Drought - 06-2026 - Anticipatory Action: Severe Drought Risk due to El Niño and Positive IOD - Indonesia 2026 ","type":"Drought","start":"2026-06-09","ccs":["id"],"affected":null,"summary":"Indonesia is forecasted to experience prolonged dry conditions during the 2026 dry season due to the combined influence of El Niño conditions and a positive Indian Ocean Dipole (IOD). According to BMKG, the dry season is expected to begin earlier than normal in many regions, with 57.2% of seasonal zones (ZOM) predicted to experience a longer dry season and 64.5% of Indonesia forecasted to receive below-normal rainfall accumulation during the June–September period. The provinces considered most a","appeals":[{"code":"MDRID030","type":"DREF","amount":120284}],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7977"},{"id":7974,"name":"Philippines: Maasim, Sarangani Earthquake, 2026","type":"Earthquake","start":"2026-06-08","ccs":["ph"],"affected":null,"summary":"At 7:37 AM on 8 June 2026, a magnitude 7.8 earthquake struck approximately 32 km south 04° west of Maasim, Sarangani, at a depth of 33 kilometers, affecting several areas in Mindanao. The Philippine Institute of Volcanology and Seismology (PHIVOLCS) recorded the strongest shaking at Intensity VII (Destructive) in General Santos City, with expected aftershocks and damages. DOST-PHIVOLCS issued Tsunami Information No. 1 on 08 June 2026 at 7:37 AM, alerting that coastal areas may experience wave he","appeals":[{"code":"MDRPH059","type":"DREF","amount":826150}],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7974"},{"id":7969,"name":"ITT: Cyclone - 06-2026 - Rain alert (ITCZ + Possible 70L formation)","type":"Cyclone","start":"2026-06-07","ccs":["cr"],"affected":null,"summary":"Based on the Informative Meteorological Warning: Watch for possible low pressure during the weekend (IMN, June 4, 2026, 9.00 am) where it is indicated that there are favorable environmental conditions for the development of a low pressure system in the Pacific maritime sector, near the coasts of Central America during the weekend, and that in addition to the above For this Thursday (June 4), the intertropical convergence zone continues to be active and close to Costa Rica, which favors an unstab","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7969"},{"id":7973,"name":"ISR: Complex Emergency - 06-2026 - Ballistic missile attack ","type":"Complex Emergency","start":"2026-06-07","ccs":["il"],"affected":null,"summary":"As of 21:55 June 7th, 2026 the Home Front command has imposed 'orange level restrictions' (limited activities) on the entire country of Israel. Beginning at 22:00 a number of missiles and missile barrages from Iran as well as Yemen were launched at various areas within Israel. Magen David Adom has activated its full war contingency plan.","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7973"},{"id":7976,"name":"SLV: Cyclone - 06-2026 - Tropical Storm Cristina ","type":"Cyclone","start":"2026-06-07","ccs":["sv"],"affected":null,"summary":"The Observatory of Hazards and Natural Resources, in its special report number 8, reports the recent formation of Tropical Storm Cristina , located approximately 161 km from the Gulf of Fonseca, with sustained winds of 72 km/h, a low central pressure of 1002 hPa and moving north at 8 km/h. it will continue to move slowly, approaching the Salvadoran coasts, favoring the dragging of moisture from the Pacific Ocean to the national territory. As a result, an increase in cloudiness and the occurrence","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7976"},{"id":7978,"name":"COD: Population displacement - 06-2026 - COD: Displacement - 06-2026 - Population movement in Lubutu Territory, Maniema Province in the Democratic Republic of Congo ","type":"Population Movement","start":"2026-06-07","ccs":["cd"],"affected":null,"summary":"The clashes broke out on Saturday, June 6, 2026 at 2:47 p.m. and continued until Sunday, June 7, 2026. It all began with the incursion of elements of the armed group known as \"Wazalendo\", placed under the command of a self-proclaimed general named Alphani Bukuy. The fighters broke into the Lazaret block, located in the Nyafanza district, in the rural commune of Lubutu, in the province of Maniema, in the east of the Democratic Republic of Congo. As soon as they arrived, they spread terror among t","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7978"},{"id":7972,"name":"ARM: Other - 06-2026 - Severe Hailstorm in Stepanavan ","type":"Other","start":"2026-06-06","ccs":["am"],"affected":null,"summary":"On 6 June 2026, at approximately 12:56 PM, a severe hailstorm struck the Stepanavan community and surrounding areas in Lori Region, Armenia. The hailstorm lasted approximately 15&ndash;20 minutes and was accompanied by exceptionally large hailstones, reportedly measuring up to 4&ndash;6 cm in diameter. The event caused extensive damage to residential properties, agricultural land, public infrastructure, vehicles, and livestock. Given the scale and severity of the impact, the Stepanavan Municipal","appeals":[{"code":"MDRAM018","type":"DREF","amount":247507}],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7972"},{"id":7970,"name":"ZMB: Epidemic - 06-2026 - Epidemic Threat ","type":"Epidemic","start":"2026-06-05","ccs":["zm"],"affected":null,"summary":"An Ebola Virus Disease (EVD) outbreak was confirmed in the Democratic Republic of Congo (DRC) and Uganda in May 2026. The outbreak involves the Bundibugyo species of Ebola, for which there is currently no approved vaccine or specific treatment, although research and clinical trials on promising candidates are ongoing. The outbreak is occurring within a complex humanitarian context characterized by insecurity, high population movement, cross-border trade, and densely populated communities, increa","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7970"},{"id":7984,"name":"COL: Drought sEAP","type":"Drought","start":"2026-06-01","ccs":["co"],"affected":null,"summary":"According to an analysis based on data provided by IDEAM, three-month precipitation forecast indicates a more than 50% probability that precipitation will be below normal, and the SPI forecast, based on a moderate drought, shows values equal to or less than 1.4 for August 2026, in large areas of the departments of Tolima and Cesar.","appeals":[{"code":"MDRCO027","type":"DREF","amount":216996}],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7984"},{"id":7968,"name":"TLS: Landslide - 06-2026 - Covalima-Landslide Response ","type":"Landslide","start":"2026-06-01","ccs":["tl"],"affected":null,"summary":"On 31 May at 11pm mid night, the moderate landslide occurred and conitnue to heavy landslide at 12-16pm on 1 June in sub village Ila, BeleCasac Village, Post Administrative Maucatar-Covalima municipality that h as impacted to 290 people . CVTL jointly with Civil Protection Authority and Civil Protection Municipality services evacuated 23 people (5 families to the 1 traditional house). based on the observation, mostly 55 houses get damaged and 21 houses totally damaged.","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7968"},{"id":7967,"name":"NGA: Storm Surge - 05-2026 - Rainstorm - Riyom, Plateau state ","type":"Storm Surge","start":"2026-05-31","ccs":["ng"],"affected":null,"summary":"On the afternoon of Sunday, 31 May 2026, a severe rainstorm accompanied by a violent windstorm swept through Tom-Gangare community in Hawan Kibo of Riyom Local Government Area, Plateau State, in Nigeria's North-Central region. The storm, which followed a prolonged and heavy downpour, generated destructive winds that tore through the rural settlement over a matter of hours, leaving a trail of widespread structural damage and deep humanitarian need in its wake. 100+ residential houses were destroy","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7967"},{"id":7954,"name":"AFG: Flood - 05-2026 - Afghanistan Flash Floods- May-2026 ","type":"Flood","start":"2026-05-25","ccs":["af"],"affected":null,"summary":"Following heavy and sustained rainfall, flash floods occurred in May 2026 across the country, affecting communities in Helmand, Herat, Uruzgan, Kunduz, Samangan, Parwan, Kapisa, Kabul, Takhar, Daikundi, Ghor, Baghlan, Sar-e-pul, Kandahar, Badakhshan, Maidan Wardak and Daikundi provinces. Low-lying areas and settlements located along riverbeds were particularly impacted. The floods resulted in loss of life, injuries, and widespread damage to shelters, livelihoods and agricultural land, reflecting","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7954"},{"id":7956,"name":"MNG: Biological Emergency - 05-2026 - Foot and mouth disease (FDM) ","type":"Biological Emergency","start":"2026-05-25","ccs":["mn"],"affected":null,"summary":"An outbreak of an infectious livestock disease, reported as foot-and-mouth disease (FMD), has been confirmed in Altai soum of Bayan-Ulgii Province. Following the confirmation, strict quarantine measures were introduced to prevent further spread of the disease. The affected area includes the Ulgii&ndash;Bugat soum&ndash;Altai soum route, where movement has been restricted. People travelling to Ulgii have been warned not to transport raw livestock products, including meat, milk, cashmere, animal h","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7956"},{"id":7957,"name":"KGZ: Pluvial/Flash Flood - 05-2026 - Mudflows in Jalal-Abad and Osh ","type":"Pluvial/Flash Flood","start":"2026-05-25","ccs":["kg"],"affected":null,"summary":"On the night of 24&ndash;25 May 2026, heavy rainfall triggered mudflows and flash floods in Osh and Jalal-Abad Oblasts in southern Kyrgyzstan. A state of emergency was declared in Manas city (Jalal-Abad Oblast) on 25 May at 04:00. No fatalities have been reported. Cleanup and recovery operations are ongoing in both oblasts. Osh Oblast A total of 15 mudflows were recorded across the oblast, affecting 313 residential buildings: 7 social infrastructure facilities damaged (3 schools, 1 kindergarten,","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7957"},{"id":7959,"name":"CHL: Earthquake - 05-2026 - MEDIUM INTENSITY EARTHQUAKE CALAMA - ANTOFAGASTA ","type":"Earthquake","start":"2026-05-25","ccs":["cl"],"affected":null,"summary":"An earthquake of medium intensity was perceived at 5:53 p.m. today, Monday, May 25, between the regions of Arica and Parinacota and Atacama, reaching a maximum perceived intensity VI Mercalli in the towns of Antofagasta, Tocopilla, Mejillones and Sierra Gorda in the Antofagasta Region. Technical background: Report of the National Seismological Center (CSN) Magnitude 6.9 MWW. Epicenter: Latitude -22.38; Longitude -68.76 Depth 114 kilometers. Geographical reference 20 kilometers northeast of Calam","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7959"},{"id":7960,"name":"BEN: Population displacement - 05-2026 - Population movement in Koulou Koualou (Matéri) ","type":"Population Movement","start":"2026-05-25","ccs":["bj"],"affected":null,"summary":"On the night of Monday 25 to Tuesday 26 May 2026, two positions of the Beninese Armed Forces were attacked in the Kourou Koualou area, on the border between Benin and Burkina Faso. These attacks have resulted in the loss of life, including among the civilian population, and have also caused a significant displacement of people to the town of Porga and other areas deemed safer. Faced with this worrying security situation, the Beninese army quickly retaliated and initiated security operations in t","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7960"},{"id":7979,"name":"IRQ: Epidemic - 05-2026 - Crimean-Congo Hemorrhagic Fever (CCHF) in Iraq/IRCS ","type":"Epidemic","start":"2026-05-24","ccs":["iq"],"affected":null,"summary":"Crimean-Congo Hemorrhagic Fever (CCHF) remains a significant public health concern in Iraq during the 2026 seasonal transmission period. The disease, which is endemic in the country, is primarily associated with exposure to infected ticks, direct contact with infected livestock, and handling of contaminated animal blood and tissues during slaughtering and meat processing activities. Iraq continues to experience seasonal increases in CCHF cases during late spring and early summer, corresponding w","appeals":[{"code":"MDRIQ021","type":"DREF","amount":280976}],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7979"},{"id":7955,"name":"TLS: Flood - 05-2026 - Flood Response-Covalima ","type":"Flood","start":"2026-05-23","ccs":["tl"],"affected":null,"summary":"Moderate to heavy rainfall was recorded on May 23, 2026 in Sikoni Village, Manatuto Municipality, and in Kasabauk, Tazhilin, and Beco Villages, Covalima Municipality. The rainfall during this period caused an increase in river water levels, which then triggered flooding in Tazhilin, Beco, and Kasabauk Villages (Covalima), as well as Sikoni Village (Manatuto). In response to this situation, Cruz Vermelha de Timor-Leste (CVTL), together with the Fire Department and CPA, immediately evacuated affec","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7955"},{"id":7958,"name":"CHL: Volcanic eruption - 05-2026 - VOLCANIC ACTIVITY NEVADOS DE LONGAVI ","type":"Volcanic Eruption","start":"2026-05-22","ccs":["cl"],"affected":null,"summary":"According to the information provided by the National Geology and Mining Service (SERNAGEOMIN), through the analysis carried out by the Volcanological Observatory of the Southern Andes (OVDAS) and product of the activity of the Nevado de Longavi volcano, On May 22, the Maule Regional Presidential Delegation, together with the regional SENAPRED, issued a basic report on the safety perimeter for the Nevado de Longaví Volcano, with background information on the technical report corresponding to SER","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7958"},{"id":7963,"name":"MDA: Pluvial/Flash Flood - 05-2026 - Flood Disaster in Ungheni and Călărași ","type":"Pluvial/Flash Flood","start":"2026-05-22","ccs":["md"],"affected":null,"summary":"The late-May 2026 floods were one of Moldova's sharpest localized hydrometeorological shocks in recent months, with Călărași and Ungheni identified by the government as the most affected districts after the torrential rains of 22 May. The damage profile was dominated by flooded households, damaged roads, pressure on dams and lakes, disrupted rail traffic, and agricultural losses. The human impact was serious but uneven: the confirmed district-level reporting shows at least one death in Călărași,","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7963"},{"id":7983,"name":"MDA: Flood - 05-2026 - Floods in Moldova May-June 2026 ","type":"Flood","start":"2026-05-22","ccs":["md"],"affected":null,"summary":"The hydrometeorological crisis that affected the Republic of Moldova from late May through mid-June 2026 caused widespread flooding and infrastructure damage across multiple regions, directly affecting an estimated 800&ndash;1,000 people. According to information from the General Inspectorate for Emergency Situations (IGSU), the National Crisis Management Center (CNMC), and local authorities, the severe weather impacted communities in 15 districts and municipalities. The first wave of torrential","appeals":[{"code":"MDRMD008","type":"DREF","amount":163942}],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7983"},{"id":7937,"name":"Africa - Ebola BVD -  Outbreak 2026","type":"Epidemic","start":"2026-05-20","ccs":["cd","ug"],"affected":null,"summary":"On 15th May, the Institut national de recherche biomédicale (INRB) Kinshasa confirmed an outbreak of the Ebola virus in Ituri province, Democratic Republic of Congo (DRC). The virus is reported to have originated from Mongbwalu, Bunia and Rwapara Health zones in Ituri province. The virus is confirmed to be the Bundibugyo Virus Disease (BVD), a severe and often fatal strain. As of 19 May , more than 500 suspected cases, including 130 suspected deaths, have been reported by the Ministry of Health.","appeals":[{"code":"MDRS1007","type":"Emergency Appeal","amount":27500000}],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7937"},{"id":7962,"name":"BULL: Civil unrest - 05-2026 - Civil unrest ","type":"Civil Unrest","start":"2026-05-20","ccs":["bo"],"affected":null,"summary":"The city of El Alto is going through an emergency situation due to the blockades and social protests registered since May 2026, which have interrupted the movement of people and goods. These disturbances have generated shortages of food, fuel and medicines, in addition to the partial suspension of educational and economic activities. The concentration of mobilizations and clashes in urban areas increases the risk to the population, affecting both the security and the living conditions of thousan","appeals":[{"code":"MDRBO022","type":"DREF","amount":154684}],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7962"},{"id":7934,"name":"ATG: Earthquake - 05-2026 - 6.5 Magnitude ","type":"Earthquake","start":"2026-05-16","ccs":["ag"],"affected":null,"summary":"A reported 6.5 magnitude earthquake was felt across Antigua and Barbuda approximately one hour ago. At this time, there have been no reports of significant damage to infrastructure, buildings, utilities, or critical services. Authorities and emergency management agencies continue to monitor the situation and conduct initial assessments where necessary. The earthquake was felt by residents across the country, with some persons briefly evacuating homes, offices, and businesses as a precautionary m","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7934"},{"id":7935,"name":"BDI: Other - 05-2026 - Bdi-Epidemic-2026 ","type":"Other","start":"2026-05-16","ccs":["bi"],"affected":null,"summary":"","appeals":[{"code":"MDRBI027","type":"DREF","amount":778787}],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7935"},{"id":7948,"name":"PER: Biological Emergency - 05-2026 - EMERGENCIA SANITARIA POR EL BROTE DE SARAMPIÓN ","type":"Biological Emergency","start":"2026-05-16","ccs":["pe"],"affected":null,"summary":"El 16 de mayo se promulg&oacute; el Decreto Supremo N&ordm; 008-2026-SA , mediante el cual se declara emergencia sanitaria por el brote de sarampi&oacute;n en el departamento de Puno y con riesgo elevado de diseminaci&oacute;n en Lima Metropolitana, as&iacute; como en los departamentos de Arequipa, Cusco, Huancavelica, Moquegua, Amazonas, Loreto, Tacna, Tumbes, Ucayali, Madre de Dios y Apur&iacute;mac, y en la Provincia Constitucional del Callao. A nivel nacional, hasta la semana epidemiol&oacut","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7948"},{"id":7947,"name":"URY: Cold Wave - 05-2026 - Red Alert for Cold Wave ","type":"Cold Wave","start":"2026-05-15","ccs":["uy"],"affected":null,"summary":"the Government of Uruguay, through the National Emergency System (SINAE), declared a Red Alert for extreme cold aimed specifically at homeless people throughout the country. The alert was activated in the face of severe cold conditions that represent a critical risk for the most vulnerable segments of the population, particularly people living on the street. The event directly impacts people without access to adequate shelter, who face life-threatening exposure to cold temperatures. As of May 19","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7947"},{"id":7924,"name":"TLS: Flood - 05-2026 - Early Action for Flood in Manufahi - TLS ","type":"Flood","start":"2026-05-12","ccs":["tl"],"affected":null,"summary":"moderate rainfall occurred two-day from Sunday 10th to 12th of May 2026 in Dotic Village Manufahi Municipality. the rain resulted overflow river inundating Dotic Village. moreover, on 12th of May 2026 National Directorate of Meteorological and Geophysics forecasted heavy intense to extreme rain from 12th to 14th of May that will likely to result raise of water level and possibility flash flood from overflow river. additionally transportation from Dotic to other village is disrupted due to the co","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7924"},{"id":7922,"name":"UGA: Flood - 05-2026 - Floods - Bukedea District - Kamutur Subcounty ","type":"Flood","start":"2026-05-11","ccs":["ug"],"affected":null,"summary":"The March April May (MAM) 2026 has been characterised by heavy rains that continue to cause floods in the low-lying areas of Uganda. On Monday, 11th May 2026, a community alert to the URCS Branch Manager in Kumi activated RCAT members to conduct a rapid assessment in Kamutur Subcounty - Bukedea District for a flood that continues to impact the vulnerable communities. The floods are reported as building from the rains and the waters from the Mt. Elgon sub-region in the neighbouring highlands. The","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7922"},{"id":7914,"name":"LBY: Complex Emergency - 05-2026 - Armed Conflicts in Zawiya","type":"Complex Emergency","start":"2026-05-08","ccs":["ly"],"affected":470000,"summary":"Violent armed conflicts begin at dawn today in Zawiya , with two armed groups and local authorities participating. This incident reflects the conflicts that took place on Friday, May 1, 2026 , and their return in a short period of time, reinforcing fears of a possible escalation of violence and a recurrence of violence in the coming days. The rapidly deteriorating security situation continues to significantly restrict secure access and data collection, making it difficult to quantify the full im","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7914"},{"id":7918,"name":"UGA: Landslide - 05-2026 - Bukimbiri-Kisoro ","type":"Landslide","start":"2026-05-06","ccs":["ug"],"affected":null,"summary":"According to the Uganda Red Cross Society the Kisoro DDMC, heavy rainfall triggered a landslide in Bukimbiri sub county causing dispalacement, destruction to crops, ,roads and death of domestic animals. The National Society is currently assessing how best to support the most vulverabe families affected by the disaster while conducting risk communication in the known high risk areas","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7918"},{"id":7919,"name":"UGA: Fire - 05-2026 - Wakiso-Busiro ","type":"Fire","start":"2026-05-05","ccs":["ug"],"affected":null,"summary":"According to the Uganda Red Cross Society , a fire outbreak gutted part of the affected area, impacting 2 households and resulting in injuries, destruction of houses, and loss of household property and personal belongings. The incident displaced affected family members and exposed them to immediate humanitarian needs, including emergency shelter, household items, and psychosocial support. The Uganda Red Cross Society, in coordination with local authorities and community leadership, conducted rap","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7919"},{"id":7909,"name":"TJK: Flood - 05-2026 - flooding and mudflows in Kulob City","type":"Flood","start":"2026-05-01","ccs":["tj"],"affected":null,"summary":"Heavy rainfall on 1 May 2026 triggered severe flooding and mudflows in Kulob City, resulting in fatalities, injuries, evacuations, and significant damage to homes and local infrastructure. Emergency response operations remain ongoing as authorities continue rescue, clean-up, and rapid damage assessments. An operational headquarters has been established at the disaster site to coordinate response efforts. The Prime Minister of the Republic of Tajikistan and the Chairman of Khatlon Region visited ","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7909"},{"id":7910,"name":"COD: Flood - 05-2026 - Floods in the town of Uvira, South Kivu province in the Democratic Republic of Congo ","type":"Flood","start":"2026-05-01","ccs":["cd"],"affected":null,"summary":"The rains that fell on the city of Uvira on May 1, 2026 at 10 a.m. in the province of South Kivu in the Democratic Republic of Congo caused material and human damage in the commune of Kalundu in the Nyamianda and Kilibula districts. This situation of flooding exacerbated by climate change and environmental degradation in the city of Uvira has been observed since 2020 by the rise of water in Lake Tanganyika and flash flooding of rivers. The Kalimabenge River flows from west to east to Lake Tangan","appeals":[{"code":"MDRCD052","type":"DREF","amount":200083}],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7910"},{"id":7906,"name":"KGZ: Flood - 04-2026 - Mudsilides - Situational report:  №. 1 ","type":"Flood","start":"2026-04-28","ccs":["kg"],"affected":null,"summary":"According to data from Kyrgyzhydromet, part of the Ministry of Emergency Situations of the Kyrgyz Republic, a series of storm warning alerts were issued between April 20 and 28, 2026. Following this on April 28, at approximately 16:45, heavy rain caused the canal in the city of Gulcha (Osh oblast) to overflow, mudsilides the areas around nearby homes. Also on the same day, around 22:30. local time, in the village of Zhashasyn, Kyz-K&ouml;l Aiyl Okmotu, Suzak District (Jalal-Abad oblast), after a","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7906"},{"id":7897,"name":"MNG: Earthquake - 04-2026 - MNG: Earthquake-04-2026 ","type":"Earthquake","start":"2026-04-26","ccs":["mn"],"affected":null,"summary":"At 12:23 on 26 April 2026 (Ulaanbaatar time), a 5.5 magnitude earthquake struck Zereg soum in Khovd province. The epicentre was located at latitude 46.90 and longitude 93.01. The earthquake was followed by a 4.2 magnitude aftershock at 12:27 PM, shortly after the initial event. This marks the third seismic event recorded in the same area within four days. On 22 April 2026, two earthquakes measuring 4.2 and 3.9 magnitudes were recorded in the region. The epicentre was located approximately: 26 km","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7897"},{"id":7915,"name":"VCT: Drought - 04-2026 - Grenadines Drought Situation ","type":"Drought","start":"2026-04-23","ccs":["vc"],"affected":null,"summary":"St. Vincent and the Grenadines has been severely impacted by the effects of climate change (National Adaptation Plan, 2019). Global climate change projections shown temperatures are expected to either continue at or near record levels in the next 5 years causing an increase in climates risks and impacts (World Meteorological Organization, 2025). According to those projections, we can expect a drier and hotter Saint Vincent and the Grenadines with less natural coastal defence structures (mangrove","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7915"},{"id":7898,"name":"PRY: Epidemic - 04-2026 - Epidemic / Outbreak of respiratory diseases (Influenza / ETI)","type":"Epidemic","start":"2026-04-22","ccs":["py"],"affected":null,"summary":"There is a sustained increase in consultations for Influenza-like Illness (INFLU-like Illness) in Paraguay, with an increase of 22% in epidemiological week 14. The event is mainly associated with the early circulation of the Influenza A H3N2 virus, at the beginning of the seasonal period. There is a risk of an increase in hospitalizations due to severe acute respiratory infections (SARI), especially in vulnerable populations, which could put pressure on health services. The sustained increase in","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7898"},{"id":7902,"name":"PRY: Flood - 04-2026 - Floods due to overflow of the Pilcomayo River – Paraguayan Chaco","type":"Flood","start":"2026-04-21","ccs":["py"],"affected":null,"summary":"In recent days, floods have been recorded in the Paraguayan Chaco region, mainly in the department of Presidente Hayes , as a result of intense rains and the overflow of the Pilcomayo River . The situation has led to flooding and isolation of communities, affecting more than 500 families and making it difficult to access basic services in vulnerable areas.","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7902"},{"id":7892,"name":"JPN: Earthquake - 04-2026 - JPN: Earthquake-04-2026-M7.7 Earthquake off the Coast of Sanriku","type":"Earthquake","start":"2026-04-20","ccs":["jp","oki"],"affected":null,"summary":"Overview A magnitude 7.7 earthquake occurred at 4:52 p.m. (local time) off the coast of Sanriku, Iwate Prefecture. A tsunami was observed; details vary by location. (The highest recorded was 80 centimeters.) A strong earthquake struck northern Japan, prompting tsunami advisories, which have now been lifted. Impact Casualties: No casualties reported at this time Damage: Some damage to buildings has been reported Lifelines: Temporary disruptions to lifelines (such as electricity and transportation","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7892"},{"id":7894,"name":"COD: Population displacement - 04-2026 - Population movement in Pangi territory, Maniema Province in the Democratic Republic of Congo. ","type":"Population Movement","start":"2026-04-20","ccs":["cd"],"affected":null,"summary":"It is since April 01, 2026 that tension has been observed in the Pangi Territory, precisely in the cities of Kampene and Kayuyu and the surrounding villages. The populations of this part woke up under a strong psychosis, at the base, the presence of elements of the Wazalendo group of the Self-proclaimed General KIWIS, who came to impose their law in contradiction to the Rega custom originating in the area. The natives, not wanting to bend to this constraint, triggered a confrontation, going as f","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7894"},{"id":7891,"name":"Malaysia: Sandakan Fire, 2026","type":"Fire","start":"2026-04-19","ccs":["my"],"affected":null,"summary":"A major fire incident occurred in the early hours at Kampung Bahagia, Batu Sapi, Sandakan, resulting in extensive destruction and significant impact on the local community. The incident, which took place at approximately 1:30 a.m., was reported to the authorities and subsequently led to the area being declared a disaster zone at 4:00 a.m. by the relevant authorities. Kampung Bahagia, a densely populated water settlement consisting of approximately 1,200 houses, was severely affected by the fire.","appeals":[{"code":"MDRMY013","type":"DREF","amount":197767}],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7891"},{"id":7900,"name":"PRY: Civil Unrest - 04-2026 - Incident at Mass Sporting Event – Superclásico (Asunción, Paraguay)","type":"Civil Unrest","start":"2026-04-19","ccs":["py"],"affected":null,"summary":"In the context of the Paraguayan soccer superclassic, incidents were recorded in the vicinity of the Defensores del Chaco Stadium , involving attendees of the event and security forces. These events led to disturbances and damage in areas near the stadium. As a result, at least 56 people were injured, including civilians and police officers, who required attention in health centers, mainly at the Barrio Obrero Hospital. The event had an immediate impact on the health of those affected, with inju","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7900"},{"id":7890,"name":"COD: Flood - 04-2026 - Floods in the province of Tshopo in the Democratic Republic of Congo ","type":"Flood","start":"2026-04-15","ccs":["cd"],"affected":null,"summary":"The torrential rains that fell throughout the province of Tshopo on Wednesday, April 15, 2026, from 10 a.m. to 2 p.m., caused flooding with losses of basic necessities. The floods have worsened following the overflows of the Congo River and some of its tributaries, namely: the Lindi and Tshopo rivers which flow into the Congo River at Kisangani, in the territory of Isangi the confluence of the Lomami River with Lokombe and in the territory of Basoko, the Aruwimi River , all these rivers have bur","appeals":[{"code":"MDRCD050","type":"DREF","amount":767376}],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7890"},{"id":7896,"name":"COD: Population displacement - 04-2026 - Population movement in Oicha capital of Beni Territory, North Kivu Province in the Democratic Republic of Congo","type":"Population Movement","start":"2026-04-15","ccs":["cd"],"affected":null,"summary":"Since October 2025, the population of the Mambanika, Tenambo, Mabasele and Kekelibo neighborhoods have moved to Oicha, the capital of Beni territory, following the resurgence of attacks by the ADF (Allied Democratic Forces) against the civilian population in Mambasa territory in Ituri province. These attacks were far from being brought under control after the carnage in Mutchatcha, but they hit several villages before hitting the center of Mambasa and advancing northwards on the Mambasa-Komanda ","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7896"},{"id":7901,"name":"PRY: Flood / flood - 04-2026 - Heavy Rains and Severe Storms","type":"Pluvial/Flash Flood","start":"2026-04-15","ccs":["py"],"affected":null,"summary":"In recent days, intense rains and severe storms have been recorded in several areas of Paraguay, generating flooding and occasional flooding in vulnerable areas of the capital and the Central department, as well as in other departments of the country. In the municipality of Limpio , the overflow of canals has affected homes in different neighborhoods, impacting at least 59 families. The situation is developing in a context of persistent climatic instability, with forecasts indicating the continu","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7901"},{"id":7886,"name":"USA: Cyclone - 04-2026 - Super Typhoon Sinlaku ","type":"Cyclone","start":"2026-04-13","ccs":["us"],"affected":null,"summary":"Tropical Cyclone Sinlaku became the world's second Category 5 tropical cyclone of 2026 at 11 a.m. EDT April 12, with 175 mph (280 km/h) winds, as rated by the Joint Typhoon Warning Center (JTWC). Sinlaku has already caused considerable damage while passing through the Western Pacific in areas including Micronesia and the Marshall Islands and is forecast to reach Guam and Commonwealth of Northern Mariana Islands (CNMI) at Category 4-equivalent strength, bringing destructive winds, heavy rainfall,","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7886"},{"id":7883,"name":"IDN: Earthquake - 04-2026 - Disaster Assessment Report: East Flores Earthquake ","type":"Earthquake","start":"2026-04-09","ccs":["id"],"affected":null,"summary":"1. Event Overview An earthquake struck East Flores Regency, East Nusa Tenggara Province, on Thursday, 9 April at 04:53 WIB. The earthquake had a magnitude of 3.7 and occurred at a depth of 10 km. The epicenter was located on land, approximately 24 km southeast of Larantuka, at coordinates 8.42&deg;S and 123.17&deg;E. 2. Seismic Activity Following the initial earthquake, several aftershocks were recorded: At 04:59 WIB, magnitude 4.0 at a depth of 3 km At 05:42 WIB, at a depth of 5 km According to","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7883"},{"id":7880,"name":"PNG: Tropical Cyclone Maila, 2026","type":"Cyclone","start":"2026-04-08","ccs":["pg"],"affected":null,"summary":"Tropical Cyclone Maila is located near 9.6˚S 156.1˚E, with its centre moving north-west at approximately 6km/hour, with maximum gusts at 296km/h. The PNG National Weather Service (NWS) has issued Tropical Cyclone Warning Number 14 (see attached), indicating that Severe Tropical Cyclone Maila (Category 5) continues to affect parts of the country. The warning remains current for Milne Bay Province, particularly coastal and island communities in Woodlark, Sudest, Misima and Rossel Islands, and Boug","appeals":[{"code":"MDRPG013","type":"DREF","amount":250000}],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7880"},{"id":7882,"name":"DOM: Pluvial Flooding / Flood - 04-2026 - Urban and Rural Flooding in Geographical Areas","type":"Pluvial/Flash Flood","start":"2026-04-07","ccs":["do"],"affected":null,"summary":"Wednesday, April 8, 2026 at 6:00 a.m. valid until Friday, April 10, 2026 at 6:00 a.m. HEAVY RAINS WILL PERSIST IN SEVERAL PROVINCES OF THE COUNTRY, DUE TO THE INCIDENCE OF A TROUGH WEATHER WARNING AND ALERT IN FORCE IN SEVERAL PROVINCES OF THE NATIONAL TERRITORY Today, Wednesday, from early in the day, we continue under favorable weather conditions for rainfall to continue in several provinces of the national territory. Consequently, continuous, moderate to heavy rains with thunderstorms, possib","appeals":[{"code":"MDRDO021","type":"DREF","amount":497829}],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7882"},{"id":7884,"name":"COD: Flood - 04-2026 - Floods in the town of Kindu, Maniema province in the DRC ","type":"Flood","start":"2026-04-07","ccs":["cd"],"affected":null,"summary":"Heavy rains have fallen in the city of Kindu, since Tuesday , March 24, 2026 have caused significant flooding, a large amount of water has been observed throughout the city, the water discharged by the city, caused the rivers running through Kindu city to flood more, leading to flooding. The event caused human and material losses, with reported damage to homes and livelihoods. The situation is made more complex by a deterioration on 07/04/2026, with the rising waters of the Congo River which con","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7884"},{"id":7875,"name":"Fiji: Tropical Cyclone Vaianu, 2026","type":"Cyclone","start":"2026-04-06","ccs":["fj"],"affected":null,"summary":"","appeals":[{"code":"MDRFJ009","type":"DREF","amount":136425}],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7875"},{"id":7878,"name":"Solomon Islands: Tropical Cyclone Maila, 2026","type":"Cyclone","start":"2026-04-06","ccs":["sb"],"affected":null,"summary":"According to the Solomon Islands Meteorological Service and community reports, s torm surge and strong winds have affected parts of Western and Choiseul Provinces. Coastal communities are experiencing sea inundation and rough conditions. Western, Choiseul, Isabel Provinces are in red alerts and Central, Malaita, Guadalcanal, Makira, Temotu, Renell & Bellona Provinces in orange alert. TC Maila category 3 is expected to intensify. Planned assessment in the next few days.","appeals":[{"code":"MDRSB007","type":"DREF","amount":281326}],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7878"},{"id":7876,"name":"COD: Population Displacement - 04-2026 - Population Movement in Kahele Territory, South Kivu Province ","type":"Population Movement","start":"2026-04-05","ccs":["cd"],"affected":null,"summary":"Since Wednesday, April 01, 2026, intense clashes have resumed in the highlands of Kalehe territory between the AFC-M23 military and the Wazalendu. The fighting was concentrated in the villages of Lumbishi, Chambombo and Shanje, and spread on Sunday, April 05, 2026 to Mwamiwidjwi, Nyamugari, Nyawaronga, Kaitolea, Kiduveri, Kashihe, Kitendebwa, Bogamanda and around Bushaku2.","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7876"},{"id":7877,"name":"COD: Flood - 04-2026 - Floods in Kahele Territory, South Kivu Province, Democratic Republic of Congo ","type":"Flood","start":"2026-04-05","ccs":["cd"],"affected":null,"summary":"Since Wednesday, April 01, 2026, intense clashes have resumed in the highlands of Kalehe territory between the AFC-M23 military and the Wazalendu. The fighting was concentrated in the villages of Lumbishi, Chambombo and Shanje, and spread on Sunday, April 05, 2026 to Mwamiwidjwi, Nyamugari, Nyawaronga, Kaitolea, Kiduveri, Kashihe, Kitendebwa, Bogamanda and around Bushaku2. In addition, in the Mbinga grouping, at the level of Bushushu, heavy rain on Sunday, April 04, 2026 caused the overflow of t","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7877"},{"id":7872,"name":"IDN: Earthquake - 04-2026 - Earthquake Incident Report in the Region Between North Maluku and North Sulawesi ","type":"Earthquake","start":"2026-04-02","ccs":["id"],"affected":null,"summary":"1. SEISMIC EVENT DATA A powerful earthquake has been recorded with the following parameters: Date (Local): April 2, 2026 Time (Local): 05:48:00 WIB Date (UTC): April 1, 2026 Time (UTC): 22:48:00 UTC Magnitude: 7.6 M Depth: 62 km Epicenter: Approx. 129 km Southeast of Bitung, North Sulawesi. 2. TSUNAMI OBSERVATIONS & THREAT ASSESSMENT Following the earthquake, a Tsunami Early Warning (Level 3) was issued. The following observations and predicted arrival times have been recorded: A. Verified Tsuna","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7872"},{"id":7873,"name":"PAK: Pluvial/Flash Flood - 04-2026 - PAK: Pluvial/Flash Flood - 04-2026 - PAK ","type":"Pluvial/Flash Flood","start":"2026-04-01","ccs":["pk"],"affected":null,"summary":"As of 4 April 2026, Pakistan is experiencing a high-alert weather situation due to an active westerly system expected to persist until 8&ndash;9 April, bringing widespread heavy rain, thunderstorms, strong winds, and snowfall in high-altitude areas. The system has already caused serious impacts, including at least 25 fatalities and dozens of injuries in Khyber Pakhtunkhwa (KP), along with the damage or destruction of over 70 houses, road disruptions, and localized flooding. Additional casualties","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7873"},{"id":7899,"name":"PRY: Epidemic - 04-2026 - Alert: Tuberculosis outbreak in prison – Concepción, Paraguay","type":"Epidemic","start":"2026-04-01","ccs":["py"],"affected":null,"summary":"The epidemiological situation in the Regional Penitentiary of Concepción has reached a critical level in April 2026, with an active outbreak of tuberculosis in the prison population. There are 58 confirmed cases under treatment and multiple deaths associated with the disease. Tuberculosis is an airborne infectious disease, whose spread is favored in closed environments, with overcrowding and limited ventilation, conditions present in the affected establishment. The event has led to the declarati","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7899"},{"id":7867,"name":"COG: Epidemic - 03-2026 - Response to the Mpox and Cholera Epidemics in Congo Brazzaville ","type":"Epidemic","start":"2026-03-31","ccs":["cg"],"affected":null,"summary":"The Africa Centres for Disease Prevention and Control have long announced that Mpox is a public health event of continental concern, while the World Health Organization (WHO) held a meeting to determine whether the current Mpox situation in Africa constitutes a Public Health Emergency of International Concern (PHEIC). The Republic of Congo has been facing cholera and mpox epidemics since July 2025, which required the activation of national public health emergency management mechanisms. As of Jul","appeals":[{"code":"MDRCG028","type":"DREF","amount":199226}],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7867"},{"id":7889,"name":"NER: Population displacement - 03-2026 - PEOPLE FORCIBLY DISPLACED IN NIGER ","type":"Population Movement","start":"2026-03-31","ccs":["ne"],"affected":null,"summary":"Since March 2025, the number of refugees and asylum seekers in Niger has increased by 1%, mainly due to registration activities. They represent 42 per cent of those of concern to UNHCR, of whom 37 per cent are refugees and 5 per cent are asylum-seekers, mainly from Nigeria (59 per cent), Mali (29 per cent) and Burkina Faso (11 per cent). Niger is home to more than 548,000 internally displaced people, or 53 per cent of the populations of concern to UNHCR, with an annual increase of 8 per cent. Th","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7889"},{"id":7862,"name":"Afghanistan: Flash Floods, 2026","type":"Flood","start":"2026-03-28","ccs":["af"],"affected":null,"summary":"Following heavy and sustained rainfall, flash floods occurred in March 2026 across the country, affecting communities in Helmand, Herat, Badghis, Uruzgan, Samangan, Laghman and Parwan provinces. Low-lying areas and settlements located along riverbeds were particularly impacted. The floods resulted in loss of life, injuries, and widespread damage to shelters, livelihoods and agricultural land, reflecting the broader pattern of seasonal flooding currently affecting several parts of the country. Ac","appeals":[{"code":"MDRAF021","type":"DREF","amount":1000001}],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7862"},{"id":7865,"name":"RUS: Flood - 03-2026 - Emergency in Dagestan Region (Russian Federation) ","type":"Flood","start":"2026-03-28","ccs":["ru"],"affected":null,"summary":"1. General Overview of the Situation Since 28 March 2026, a complex flood situation has persisted in the Republic of Dagestan, caused by heavy rainfall and strong gusty winds. The most affected areas include Makhachkala, the Khasavyurt district, Derbent, and a number of municipalities across the republic. As of 30 March, the situation has begun to stabilize; however, recovery and emergency response operations continue in certain areas. 2. Scale of the Emergency A state of emergency has been decl","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7865"},{"id":7853,"name":"TZA: Landslide - 03-2026 - Rungwe Flood and Landslide ","type":"Landslide","start":"2026-03-25","ccs":["tz"],"affected":null,"summary":"Heavy and persistent rainfall in Rungwe District has triggered a deadly landslide affecting several wards, including Nkunga, Lupepo, Kawetele, and Ikuti. According to an official statement issued by the Regional Police Commander of Mbeya Region, the incident has resulted in 18 fatalities , including 14 children , with additional reports of injuries and missing persons. Effects of the hazard The landslide has caused widespread destruction of homes and infrastructure, burying houses and personal b","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7853"},{"id":7855,"name":"COD: Flooding - 03-2026 - Floods in Bukama Territory, Haut Lomami Province ","type":"Flood","start":"2026-03-25","ccs":["cd"],"affected":null,"summary":"Since March 3, heavy rains have fallen in the territory of Bukama, precisely in the city of Bukama in the Province of Haut-Lomami. These have caused flooding in 6 of the 18 existing districts. It has also caused erosion, destruction of homes and loss of life.","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7855"},{"id":7858,"name":"IRQ: Pluvial/Flash Flood - 03-2026 - IRAQ: havey rains ","type":"Pluvial/Flash Flood","start":"2026-03-25","ccs":["iq"],"affected":null,"summary":"The country is currently (late March 2026) experiencing a heavy rainfall wave encompassing most governorates. According to the latest data issued by the General Authority for Meteorology and Seismic Monitoring and observational reports up to March 26, 2026, Details of recorded rainfall amounts (in millimeters) during the past 12 to 24 hours: Recorded rainfall amounts in the governorates (March 25-26, 2026) The amounts varied between moderate and heavy, and the preliminary estimates were as follo","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7858"},{"id":7850,"name":"LBR: Other - 03-2026 - Tensions between Liberia - Guinea Border in Lofa County ","type":"Other","start":"2026-03-24","ccs":["lr"],"affected":null,"summary":"On March 2, 2026, Guinean soldiers seized equipment owned by BK Enterprise, a Liberian company mining sand on the Makona River, claiming mineral extraction and ownership of the river. Despite intervention by Liberia's Minister of Internal Affairs, tensions escalated when Guinean soldiers hoisted Guinean national flag on Liberian soil on March 10, later removed by local youths. A MRU Heads of State meeting on March 16 produced a communiqu&eacute; committing to peace, security, and respect for ter","appeals":[{"code":"MDRLR010","type":"DREF","amount":376240}],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7850"},{"id":7854,"name":"COD: Flood - 03-2026 - Floods in Kindu City, Manième Province ","type":"Flood","start":"2026-03-24","ccs":["cd"],"affected":null,"summary":"A torrential rain fell in the city of Kindu on Tuesday 24/03/2026, from 07:00 local time, and it lasted only 2 hours at most, a large amount of water was observed throughout the city. However, the amount of water discharged by the latter caused the rivers crossing the city to flood more; flood observed by the overflow of the waters from their usual beds. The damage recorded was more limited to the loss of household property, the collapse of some residential houses, cracks in the walls, etc., wer","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7854"},{"id":7856,"name":"COD: Flood - 03-2026 - floods in the city of Gbadolite province of Nord-Ubangi ","type":"Flood","start":"2026-03-24","ccs":["cd"],"affected":null,"summary":"In the afternoon of Tuesday 24/03/2026, torrential rain fell from 5 p.m. in the city of Gbadolite causing a lot of material damage and loss of human life. It should be noted that the city of Gbadolite has three communes below : the commune of Gbadolite, the commune of Nganza and the commune of Molegbe.","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7856"},{"id":7859,"name":"LBR: Storm Surge - 03-2026 - Liberia_Storms in Lofa and Nimba ","type":"Storm Surge","start":"2026-03-24","ccs":["lr"],"affected":null,"summary":"Between March 19&ndash;24, 2026, violent windstorms struck communities across Nimba and Lofa Counties in Liberia, severely damaging fragile housing structures and displacing families. A total of 213 households occupied by approximately 3,704 people were directly affected. The storms affected six communities in Nimba and five in Lofa, leaving families exposed to harsh weather conditions and without basic household items. Vulnerable groups, including women, children, the elderly, pregnant women, a","appeals":[],"link":"https://go.ifrc.org/emergencies/7859"}],"note":"150 emergencies"};
